{{Basis}}

The '''automotive industry in Qym''' is one of the most prominent and largest industries on [[Basis]]. In {{abbr|2440|2027 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}, Qym produced 7,136,394 motor vehicles, ranking as the [[List of countries on Basis by motor vehicle production|second largest producer on Basis]]. That same year, there were 83,615,184 registered motor vehicles, making Qym the [[List of countries and territories on Basis by motor vehicles per capita|third largest automotive market on Basis]]. 

Qym is home to three major automotive manufacturers: 
*[[Cajech]], ran by the [[Cajech family]], is headquartered in [[Tulim]] and produced around 3.3 million vehicles in Qym<!--9 million globally--> in {{abbr|2440|2027 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}. 
*[[Tarez]], ran by the [[Tarez family]], is headquartered in [[Patsalys]] and produced around 2.2 million vehicles in Qym<!--3 million globally--> in {{abbr|2440|2027 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}. 
*[[Marnyj]], ran by the [[Marnyj family]], is headquartered in [[Leramy]] and produced around 1.5 million vehicles in Qym<!--3 million globally--> in {{abbr|2440|2027 (Earth Year Equivalent)}}. 

Other minor automotive manufacturers exist but have a marginal impact on the Qymish automotive industry at large, producing less than 100,000 units combined yearly. In terms of auto parts manufacturers, [[Prykras]] and [[Istovody]] are by far the largest and major players globally. 

